# Crow — Project Overview

Crow is an open-source AI coding agent that brings AI assistance directly into the terminal. It works with any OpenAI-compatible provider: 206 built-in providers plus a custom provider wizard for any other endpoint.

## Tech Stack

- **Language**: TypeScript (ES2022, ESNext modules)
- **Runtime**: Bun (primary)
- **UI Framework**: React with [OpenTUI](https://github.com/anomalyco/opentui) for terminal rendering
- **Build**: `tsc` (TypeScript compiler)
- **Package Manager**: Bun
- **Model layer**: Vercel AI SDK (`ai` + `@ai-sdk/openai`, Chat Completions only)
- **Storage**: `bun:sqlite` (sessions, transcripts, thoughts)
- **Tools**: File, bash, grep, computer control, MCP servers, LSP, subagents

## Architecture

```
src/
├── index.ts          # CLI entry point (Commander.js + OpenTUI)
├── agent/
│   ├── agent.ts      # Agent coordinator, session management, subagent routing
│   ├── delegations.ts # Background delegations (explore-only)
│   ├── reasoning.ts  # Reasoning handling, encrypted-reasoning filtering
│   └── compaction.ts # Conversation compaction
├── crow/
│   ├── client.ts     # Provider runtime (createOpenAI, reasoning capture)
│   ├── models.ts     # Model definitions and metadata
│   └── tools.ts      # Tool schemas (bash, read, grep, task, delegate, computer)
├── tools/
│   ├── bash.ts       # Bash command execution
│   ├── file.ts       # File read/edit
│   ├── grep.ts       # Ripgrep-backed search
│   └── computer.ts   # Desktop screenshot/input tools
├── ui/
│   ├── app.tsx       # OpenTUI React terminal UI
│   └── agents-modal.tsx # Sub-agent browser and editor
├── utils/
│   ├── settings.ts   # User and project settings
│   ├── providers.ts  # Built-in provider catalog and live model fetch
│   ├── agent-files.ts # Markdown sub-agent registry (.crow/agents)
│   └── skills.ts     # Skill discovery
├── storage/          # SQLite transcript, sessions, thoughts tables
├── mcp/              # MCP server runtime
├── lsp/              # LSP client
├── telegram/         # Telegram bridge
├── verify/           # Verification recipes and orchestration
└── types/
    └── index.ts      # Shared TypeScript types
```

## Key Patterns

- **Agent loop**: `Agent.processMessage()` is an async generator that yields `StreamChunk` objects — the LLM responds, tools execute, results feed back until no more tool calls remain or `maxToolRounds` is reached.
- **Tools**: Built with `tool()` + zod schemas. Tools return `ToolResult` and never throw.
- **Subagents**: `subagent` runs an agent in a child session (foreground by default, `background=true` for async runs, `sessionID` for follow-ups). Agents are defined by Markdown files (project `.crow/agents/` > global `~/.crow/agents/` > settings customs > six built-ins: explorer, builder, reviewer, tester, planner, general-purpose). Child sessions persist in the sessions table with a parent link.
- **Thought persistence**: Provider reasoning is captured from the raw SSE stream (the AI SDK drops `reasoning_content` in chat completions), stored per turn with its duration, and shown in history as a clickable Thought line.
- **Providers**: 206 built-in OpenAI-compatible providers. Keys are saved by `/connect` to `~/.crow/auth.json` (mode 600). A custom provider can be added with any base URL, key, and model.
- **Settings hierarchy**: Environment variables (`CROW_PROVIDER`, `CROW_MODEL`, `CROW_MAX_TOKENS`) → User-level (`~/.crow/user-settings.json`) → Project-level (`.crow/settings.json`).
- **Custom instructions**: `~/.crow/AGENTS.md`, then `AGENTS.override.md` / `AGENTS.md` per directory from git root through the workspace cwd (Codex-style merge).
- **ESM only**: The project uses `"type": "module"` — all imports use `.js` extensions for compiled output.

## CI/CD

- **typecheck.yml**: Runs `tsc --noEmit` on push/PR to `main`/`develop`.
- **security.yml**: Runs `npm audit` and TruffleHog secret scanning.
- **release.yml**: Runs on `crow@*` tags and publishes Linux, macOS, and Windows binaries.
